NAME
    ls - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
    ls [-a] [-l] [-al | -la] [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Lists entries of [path] (default: current directory) inside the
    shell sandbox, one entry per line in ordinal name order. Directory
    names carry a trailing '/' in short format. When [path] names a
    single file, prints that file's entry.

OPTIONS
    -a  Include entries starting with '.'.
    -l  Long format: entry type ('d' or '-'), byte size (0 for
        directories), local modification timestamp, and name.
    -al, -la
        Combine -a and -l.

EXAMPLES
    ls
    ls -la /Logs
    ls -l /Games

EXIT STATUS
    0   Listing printed.
    1   Path outside sandbox or path does not exist.

SEE ALSO
    find(1), cd(1), pwd(1), hier(7)
